        <h2 class="heading-lg measure">AI receptionist vs. live answering: an honest comparison</h2>
        <p>Both models exist in Fayetteville, and we will tell you when the cheaper one is enough.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Live answering service.</strong> A human operator answers, takes a message,
          and relays it. Strength: a person handles anything unexpected. Weakness: you pay per
          minute or per call, operators read from a script they did not write, and the work of
          booking still comes back to your desk the next morning. National providers serving
          Arkansas list entry tiers from $25 to $44 a month, with per-minute billing above the
          included allowance (<a class="text-link" href="https://www.receptionhq.com/arkansas-answering-service" rel="noopener">ReceptionHQ, from $25/month</a>;
          <a class="text-link" href="https://specialtyansweringservice.net/answering-service-arkansas" rel="noopener">Specialty Answering Service, from $44/mo</a>;
          entry-tier list prices as of September 2026).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI receptionist.</strong> Software answers in your voice, qualifies by your
          rules, and books during the call. Strength: flat monthly cost, identical handling at
          2 p.m. and 2 a.m., every call recorded. Weakness: it does not improvise outside its
          rules, and callers with emotional or unusual situations are better served by a human,
          so you keep the escalation path.
        </p>
